 | `nodepool[].annotations` | none | passed onto the NodePool as written, values as strings, next to the chart's own sync-wave (which an entry may not set). The workflows' update-nodepool reads `redbull.io/scale-down-policy` (`fewest-pods`, `least-requested`, `least-utilized`) from it |
 | `nodepool[].additionalInfraEnvNames` | unset | Agent platform: more InfraEnvs the NodePool may draw Agents from (below) |
+| `excludeAgentLabels` | unset | Agent platform: label keys no NodePool of the cluster takes an Agent with (below); set in any values file |
+| `nodepool[].excludeAgentLabels` | unset | more keys for that nodepool, added to `excludeAgentLabels` |
 
 **A nodepool may draw from several InfraEnvs.** With `additionalInfraEnvNames`, the
 NodePool's `agentLabelSelector` is one `matchExpressions` requirement,
@@ -276,6 +278,34 @@ node. The render fails on KubeVirt, and with the legacy
 demand only from a single `matchLabels`, so it skips one with this selector ("not
 tied to an InfraEnv") and orders no servers for it.
 
+**Agents carrying a label can be kept out.** Each key in `excludeAgentLabels`
+(the chart-wide list) and in a nodepool's own `excludeAgentLabels` becomes a
+`{key: <key>, operator: DoesNotExist}` requirement in the NodePool's
+`agentLabelSelector`, next to its `matchLabels` (one InfraEnv) or after its `In`
+requirement (several), sorted and unique. A NodePool then never takes an Agent
+that carries the label. The use is herzi's collector of used Agents: herzi labels
+every Agent installed in a cluster as used, since an uninstall or a scale-down does
+not return a used Agent to the inventory cleanly, and deletes a free Agent that
+carries the label. Every NodePool excluding that label keeps a freed used Agent from
+being bound again before herzi deletes it. The label's name is herzi's to choose,
+so the chart takes any list of label keys. The chart-wide list can be
+set in any values file (`sites/configValues.yaml`, a site's, an MCE's or a cluster
+file); Helm replaces a list, so the most specific file that sets it wins, and a
+nodepool's own keys add to it. Unset or empty, the selector is exactly what it was.
+Agent platform only: a KubeVirt nodepool skips the chart-wide list, and its own
+list fails the render. The render also fails on a key that is not a label key and
+on the label the NodePool selects its InfraEnv by. herzi (on its main today) reports
+a NodePool whose `matchLabels` has any `matchExpressions` beside it as a problem of
+its InfraEnv's pool ("selector must be only the InfraEnv label"), and a pool with a
+problem orders no servers at all, for any cluster. So add an exclusion only once
+herzi accepts it, and on MCEs whose pools herzi does not fill until then.
+
+**Changing a NodePool's selector** (`additionalInfraEnvNames` or
+`excludeAgentLabels`, at any layer) touches no running node on an `InPlace`
+NodePool, the default: the Agent provider reads the selector only when a new Machine claims an
+Agent, so the nodes it already has stay. On a `Replace` NodePool the same change is
+a new machine template, and HyperShift replaces every node, one by one.
+
 `releaseRepo` (and `cpoRepo`) must describe the same layout as the upgrade rules'
 `release` block in the values repo (`upgrade/ladder.yaml`): the upgrade workflow
 builds and pins the image references from the rules, Argo CD renders them from here.
diff --git a/templates/nodepool.yaml b/templates/nodepool.yaml
index 3c376fd..470aad8 100644
--- a/templates/nodepool.yaml
+++ b/templates/nodepool.yaml
@@ -66,6 +66,42 @@
 {{- end }}
 {{- end }}
 {{- end }}
+{{- /* excludeAgentLabels: label keys an Agent must not carry for this NodePool to take
+       it, the chart-wide list (any values file; Helm replaces a list, so the most
+       specific file that sets it wins) plus the nodepool's own, sorted and unique,
+       each a DoesNotExist requirement next to the InfraEnv one. herzi's collector of
+       used Agents needs it: a freed Agent carrying its "used" label is never bound
+       again before herzi deletes it. Agent platform only:
+       a KubeVirt nodepool skips the chart-wide list and fails on its own. Unset or
+       empty: the selector is exactly what it was. */}}
+{{- $excludeAll := $.Values.excludeAgentLabels | default list }}
+{{- if not (kindIs "slice" $excludeAll) }}
+{{- fail "excludeAgentLabels must be a list of label keys." }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- $excludeOwn := .excludeAgentLabels | default list }}
+{{- if not (kindIs "slice" $excludeOwn) }}
+{{- fail (printf "nodepool %q: excludeAgentLabels must be a list of label keys." $name) }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- if and $excludeOwn (eq $platform "kubevirt") }}
+{{- fail (printf "nodepool %q: excludeAgentLabels is for the agent platform; a KubeVirt nodepool selects no Agent." $name) }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- $exclude := list }}
+{{- if ne $platform "kubevirt" }}
+{{- $exclude = concat $excludeAll $excludeOwn | uniq }}
+{{- $selectedBy := "infraenvs.agent-install.openshift.io" }}
+{{- if not $more }}
+{{- $selectedBy = $selector.nodeLabelKey | default $selectedBy }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- range $exclude }}
+{{- if not (and (kindIs "string" .) (regexMatch `^([a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?(\.[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?)*/)?[A-Za-z0-9]([-A-Za-z0-9_.]{0,61}[A-Za-z0-9])?$` .)) }}
+{{- fail (printf "nodepool %q: every excludeAgentLabels entry must be a label key (such as example.com/used), not %v." $name .) }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- if eq . $selectedBy }}
+{{- fail (printf "nodepool %q: excludeAgentLabels may not name %s, the label the NodePool selects its InfraEnv by; it would take no Agent." $name .) }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- end }}
+{{- $exclude = sortAlpha $exclude }}
+{{- end }}
 {{- /* hasKey rather than default throughout: an explicit 0 or false must win. */}}
 {{- $replicas := ternary .replicas 1 (hasKey . "replicas") | int }}
 {{- $allowDeletion := ternary $labels.allowDeletion "false" (hasKey $labels "allowDeletion") }}
@@ -156,9 +192,20 @@ spec:
           {{- range concat (list $infraEnv) $more | uniq | sortAlpha }}
           - {{ . | quote }}
           {{- end }}
+        {{- range $exclude }}
+        - key: {{ . | quote }}
+          operator: DoesNotExist
+        {{- end }}
         {{- else }}
         matchLabels:
           {{ $selector.nodeLabelKey | default "infraenvs.agent-install.openshift.io" }}: {{ $infraEnv }}
+        {{- with $exclude }}
+        matchExpressions:
+        {{- range . }}
+        - key: {{ . | quote }}
+          operator: DoesNotExist
+        {{- end }}
+        {{- end }}
         {{- end }}
     type: Agent
   {{- end }}
diff --git a/tests/test_nodepool_exclude_agent_labels.py b/tests/test_nodepool_exclude_agent_labels.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c334453
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/test_nodepool_exclude_agent_labels.py
@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+"""Agents carrying a label are kept out of a NodePool: excludeAgentLabels.
+
+Each key of the chart-wide excludeAgentLabels and of a nodepool's own
+excludeAgentLabels is a {key, operator: DoesNotExist} requirement in the
+NodePool's agentLabelSelector, sorted and unique, next to the InfraEnv one. The
+point: herzi labels every Agent installed in a cluster as used and deletes a free
+Agent that carries the label; a NodePool that excludes the label never binds a
+freed used Agent again before herzi deletes it. The label's name is herzi's, so
+the key here is a placeholder. Properties, each of which would fail quietly if
+broken:
+
+1. Unset or empty, the render is byte for byte what it was, so every cluster file
+   in the values repo renders as before.
+2. The chart-wide list reaches every Agent NodePool; a nodepool's own keys add to it.
+3. It sits next to matchLabels (one InfraEnv) or after the In requirement (several,
+   additionalInfraEnvNames), and the NodePool keeps its name.
+4. KubeVirt nodepools select no Agent: the chart-wide list leaves them as they are,
+   their own list fails.
+5. A key that is not a label key, or the label the InfraEnv is selected by, fails.
+
+On an InPlace NodePool (the default) a changed selector touches no running node;
+on a Replace NodePool the same change replaces every node.
+
+Requirements: helm CLI on PATH (module-level skip marker).
+"""
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import pytest
+import yaml
+
+CHART = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
+FIXTURES = CHART / "tests" / "fixtures" / "hostedcluster"
+LABEL = "infraenvs.agent-install.openshift.io"
+MARK = "example.com/used"
+
+pytestmark = pytest.mark.skipif(shutil.which("helm") is None, reason="helm CLI not available")
+
+
+def _helm(fixture: str, *args: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
+    return subprocess.run(
+        ["helm", "template", "t", str(CHART), "--set-string", "clusterName=tenant-a",
+         "-f", str(FIXTURES / f"{fixture}.yaml"), *args],
+        capture_output=True, text=True,
+    )
+
+
+def _ok(fixture: str, *args: str) -> str:
+    r = _helm(fixture, *args)
+    assert r.returncode == 0, r.stderr
+    return r.stdout
+
+
+def _pools(*args: str, fixture: str = "production-agent") -> dict[str, dict]:
+    docs = [d for d in yaml.safe_load_all(_ok(fixture, *args)) if d]
+    return {d["metadata"]["name"]: d for d in docs if d["kind"] == "NodePool"}
+
+
+def _selector(pool: dict) -> dict:
+    return pool["spec"]["platform"]["agent"]["agentLabelSelector"]
+
+
+def _out(*keys: str) -> list[dict]:
+    return [{"key": k, "operator": "DoesNotExist"} for k in keys]
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("fixture", ["production-agent", "production-kubevirt-external", "lab-kubevirt-local"])
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("empty", ["excludeAgentLabels=[]", "excludeAgentLabels=null", "nodepool[0].excludeAgentLabels=[]"])
+def test_unset_or_empty_renders_byte_for_byte_as_before(fixture, empty):
+    assert _ok(fixture, "--set-json", empty) == _ok(fixture)
+
+
+def test_the_chart_wide_list_reaches_every_agent_nodepool_next_to_match_labels():
+    pools = _pools("--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]')
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-zone-a"]) == {
+        "matchLabels": {LABEL: "dell-r660-128c-1024gb"}, "matchExpressions": _out(MARK),
+    }
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-hp-dl380-64c-512gb"]) == {
+        "matchLabels": {LABEL: "hp-dl380-64c-512gb"}, "matchExpressions": _out(MARK),
+    }
+
+
+def test_a_nodepools_own_keys_add_to_the_chart_wide_list_sorted_and_unique():
+    pools = _pools(
+        "--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]',
+        "--set-json", f'nodepool[1].excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}", "a.example.com/hold", "zz"]',
+    )
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-hp-dl380-64c-512gb"])["matchExpressions"] == _out("a.example.com/hold", MARK, "zz")
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-zone-a"])["matchExpressions"] == _out(MARK)
+
+
+def test_a_nodepools_own_keys_need_no_chart_wide_list():
+    pools = _pools("--set-json", f'nodepool[0].excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]')
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-zone-a"])["matchExpressions"] == _out(MARK)
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-hp-dl380-64c-512gb"]) == {"matchLabels": {LABEL: "hp-dl380-64c-512gb"}}
+
+
+def test_with_several_infraenvs_the_exclusions_follow_the_in_requirement():
+    pools = _pools(
+        "--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]',
+        "--set-string", "nodepool[1].additionalInfraEnvNames={aa-infraenv}",
+    )
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-hp-dl380-64c-512gb"]) == {
+        "matchExpressions": [
+            {"key": LABEL, "operator": "In", "values": ["aa-infraenv", "hp-dl380-64c-512gb"]},
+            *_out(MARK),
+        ]
+    }
+
+
+def test_the_nodepools_keep_their_names_and_all_but_the_selector():
+    before = _pools()
+    after = _pools("--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]')
+    assert set(after) == set(before)
+    for name, pool in after.items():
+        del pool["spec"]["platform"]["agent"], before[name]["spec"]["platform"]["agent"]
+        assert pool == before[name]
+
+
+def test_with_the_legacy_node_label_key_the_exclusions_sit_next_to_it():
+    pools = _pools(
+        "--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]',
+        "--set-string", "nodepool[1].agentLabelSelector.nodeLabelKey=legacy.example/pool",
+        "--set-string", "nodepool[1].agentLabelSelector.nodeLabelValue=hp-dl380-64c-512gb",
+    )
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-hp-dl380-64c-512gb"]) == {
+        "matchLabels": {"legacy.example/pool": "hp-dl380-64c-512gb"}, "matchExpressions": _out(MARK),
+    }
+
+
+def test_keys_that_read_as_other_types_stay_strings():
+    pools = _pools("--set-string", "excludeAgentLabels={true,1234}")
+    assert _selector(pools["tenant-a-zone-a"])["matchExpressions"] == _out("1234", "true")
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("fixture", ["production-kubevirt-external", "lab-kubevirt-local"])
+def test_kubevirt_skips_the_chart_wide_list(fixture):
+    assert _ok(fixture, "--set-json", f'excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]') == _ok(fixture)
+
+
+def test_kubevirt_fails_on_a_nodepools_own_list():
+    r = _helm("lab-kubevirt-local", "--set-json", f'nodepool[0].excludeAgentLabels=["{MARK}"]')
+    assert r.returncode != 0
+    assert "excludeAgentLabels is for the agent platform" in r.stderr
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("value, message", [
+    ("excludeAgentLabels=\"example.com/used\"", "excludeAgentLabels must be a list of label keys"),
+    ("nodepool[1].excludeAgentLabels=\"example.com/used\"", "excludeAgentLabels must be a list of label keys"),
+    ('excludeAgentLabels=["example.com/used=true"]', "every excludeAgentLabels entry must be a label key"),
+    ('excludeAgentLabels=[""]', "every excludeAgentLabels entry must be a label key"),
+    ('excludeAgentLabels=[3]', "every excludeAgentLabels entry must be a label key"),
+    ('excludeAgentLabels=["Example.COM/used"]', "every excludeAgentLabels entry must be a label key"),
+    (f'excludeAgentLabels=["{LABEL}"]', "may not name infraenvs.agent-install.openshift.io"),
+])
+def test_a_wrong_value_fails(value, message):
+    r = _helm("production-agent", "--set-json", value)
+    assert r.returncode != 0
+    assert message in r.stderr
+
+
+def test_the_legacy_selector_label_may_not_be_excluded():
+    r = _helm(
+        "production-agent",
+        "--set-string", "nodepool[1].agentLabelSelector.nodeLabelKey=legacy.example/pool",
+        "--set-string", "nodepool[1].agentLabelSelector.nodeLabelValue=hp-dl380-64c-512gb",
+        "--set-json", 'nodepool[1].excludeAgentLabels=["legacy.example/pool"]',
+    )
+    assert r.returncode != 0
+    assert "may not name legacy.example/pool" in r.stderr
